#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cumulant

#% text
# `cumulant(data, r)` gives the r-th cumulant of the list `data`, computed from its raw moments.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The recurrence is `kappa(r) = m(r) - sum over k < r of binomial(r - 1, k - 1) kappa(k) m(r - k)` with `m` the raw moments of the data.

#% item
# The first cumulant is the mean and the second the biased variance.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cumulant([1, 2, 3, 4, 7], 1)
#% output
#= 17/5

#% cell
cumulant([1, 2, 3, 4, 7], 2)
#% output
#= 106/25

#% cell
cumulant([1, 2, 3, 4, 7], 3)
#% output
#= 756/125

#% cell
cumulant([1, 2, 3, 4, 7], 2) == variance([1, 2, 3, 4, 7])*4/5
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `moment`, `central_moment`, `variance`, `kurtosis`
